invariant: INV-14
file: cpu_cfg.h
catches: test/host-builds.sh
reason: cpu_cfg.h's x86-64 set loses CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256, so every
  init call of an x86-64 object refuses a caller that states the SHA
  extensions, and no x86-64 session can run SHA-256 on them
  (docs/decisions.md 93). On arm64 no test row moves, because that set is
  unchanged, so the catch is the script, which reads the header for both
  architectures and compares each set with the bits it writes out.

--- old
     CH_CPU_VAES | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 | CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA)
--- new
     CH_CPU_VAES | CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA)
